Leadership Reflections: Working Smart

Keep learning! Competent professionals are always trying to work in a way that’s efficient, effective, or in this case, smart. We often think of working smart as making efficient choices and picking the right objectives. Pat took this aspiration further, suggesting that the only way that you can work smart is to consistently challenge yourself to fuel your mind with insights and innovations that shape your journey. This includes:

committing to growing;

establishing and connecting with mentors;

learning from your peers, colleagues, and competitors; and

committing to professional learning.
